est.config.ts\",\"reason\":\"exclude the new cli-process-mutations suite outside LHC_PROCESS_SUITE=1, matching the other process suites\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/mutations.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-5.1 through TC-5.5 plus the induced-failure atomicity leg and a background-mode edit-and-walk-away production-path test\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/cli-process-mutations.test.ts\",\"reason\":\"NEW: TC-5.6 SDK/CLI twin parity (result JSON, cascade rows, read-back) plus CLI refusal parity\"},{\"path\":\"packages/lhc/test/red-manifest.json\",\"reason\":\"recorded the two new test files' hashes (green may add files; the record step locks them)\"}],\"tests\":{\"added\":[\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.1: synchronous content/blocks/estimate update, cleared + queued named on the result, rebuild derives from edited content\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.1 atomicity (architecture risk): induced cascade failure (planted claimed row at the replacement id) rolls back the content change too; full snapshot byte-stable\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.2 (architecture risk): two-chunk thread, cleared set exactly 5 forms (message + turn's 2 + chunk 1's 2); every form outside the chain deep-equal pre-edit including source version\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.3: post-return all dependents pending, replacement ids carry the new source version; second edit supersedes the still-queued first wave, rows deleted, ids reported\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.4 (epic's named architecture-risk test): delayed double holds a claimed pre-edit smoothing across the edit; old and replacement items coexist (version-scoped ids); drain report shows stale_discarded then done; exactly one ready row from post-edit content\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — TC-5.5: turn_open and message_not_found refusals plus deleted-target-reads-as-message_not_found; snapshot (messages + forms + queue) identical after each\",\"test/mutations.test.ts — background-mode edit-and-walk-away: cascade pokes ride