te.ts and `lhc messages edit --message/--message-id --content` wiring with parity proven through the spawned binary.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:354:    planSummary: \"Implemented the turns derivation layer (Story 3, TC-3.1–3.9). Added a completion-transaction hook to the work-queue util (complete() gains an optional onApplied callback invoked inside the completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, only when the version-checked form writes hit, with onCommit registrations flushed post-commit) so chunk placement and the close→summary enqueues ride the same commit as the rendering/projection writes — the story's placement-atomicity requirement — while the util stays domain-blind. New turns-internal modules: compose.ts (pure (messages, forms) → {parts, gaps}: ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content with one DependencyGap per fallback, tool parts carry mechanically derived outcomes in message order so a run's outcome structurally cannot be lost), chunks.ts (placeTurn with the DD-9 accumulated close policy — close when accumulated + incoming ≥ target excluding the incoming turn, single projection ≥ max self-chunks immediately, empty chunks never close, already-placed turns keep their placement on rebuild — plus enqueueChunkSummaries and placement read-back), forms.ts (deleted-filtered turn/member/form/projection reads), derive.ts (turn_derivation handler: compose → composeTurnRendering → projectLowerBand → two form writes + placement hook with estimateTokens computed exactly once at landing; chunk_summary_detailed/brief handlers reading member projections in member_idx order). Registered turns.workHandlers; turn read-back now carries chunkId/memberIdx. Gaps are recorded facts: repair of a dependency changes nothing (TC-3.3 byte-equal assertion); explicit re-queues in tests drive the queue util directly per the story note.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:379:        reason: \"complete() accepts the onApplied hook: runs inside the completion transaction after non-stale form writes; commit hooks flush after COMMIT, drop on rollback\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-002.md:382:        reason: \"drain passes outcome.onApplied through to complete()\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:450:    planSummary: \"Implemented the turns derivation layer (Story 3, TC-3.1–3.9). Added a completion-transaction hook to the work-queue util (complete() gains an optional onApplied callback invoked inside the completion's BEGIN IMMEDIATE, only when the version-checked form writes hit, with onCommit registrations flushed post-commit) so chunk placement and the close→summary enqueues ride the same commit as the rendering/projection writes — the story's placement-atomicity requirement — while the util stays domain-blind. New turns-internal modules: compose.ts (pure (messages, forms) → {parts, gaps}: ready forms verbatim, non-ready fall back to raw/truncated content with one DependencyGap per fallback, tool parts carry mechanically derived outcomes in message order so a run's outcome structurally cannot be lost), chunks.ts (placeTurn with the DD-9 accumulated close policy — close when accumulated + incoming ≥ target excluding the incoming turn, single projection ≥ max self-chunks immediately, empty chunks never close, already-placed turns keep their placement on rebuild — plus enqueueChunkSummaries and placement read-back), forms.ts (deleted-filtered turn/member/form/projection reads), derive.ts (turn_derivation handler: compose → composeTurnRendering → projectLowerBand → two form writes + placement hook with estimateTokens computed exactly once at landing; chunk_summary_detailed/brief handlers reading member projections in member_idx order). Registered turns.workHandlers; turn read-back now carries chunkId/memberIdx. Gaps are recorded facts: repair of a dependency changes nothing (TC-3.3 byte-equal assertion); explicit re-queues in tests drive the queue util directly per the story note.\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:475:        reason: \"complete() accepts the onApplied hook: runs inside the completion transaction after non-stale form writes; commit hooks flush after COMMIT, drop on rollback\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/03-turn-composition-chunk-formation/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-006.md:478:        reason: \"drain passes outcome.onApplied through to complete()\"\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/prompts/001-planner-turn-005.md:441:    planSummary: \"Implemented Story 5 (message edit and cascade): a new shared cascade module (src/domains/messages/internal/cascade.ts) derives the clear-set structurally from the message → turn → chunk walk over existing derived_form rows, supersede-deletes still-queued old-version items (reported on the result), and enqueues replacements at each group's max source version + 1 inside the mutation's transaction. messages.edit validates through the deleted-filtered read (turn_open / message_not_found refusals), applies content + blocks + token re-stamp via new store.ts helpers (readMutableMessage / applyMessageEdit mirroring projectEvent's counted fields), runs the cascade, and returns the MutationResult — one synchronous commit, with enqueue pokes riding onCommit so background mode rebuilds with no further call. The source-version check (existing single write path in work-queue complete()) is provoked by TC-5.4's delayed-double recipe: a real claimed pre-edit item held across the edit completes after the post-edit replacement is queued and discards as stale_discarded. CLI: new src/cli/messages-mutate.ts and `lhc messages edit --message/--message-id --content` wiring with parity proven through the spawned binary.\"\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:14:The epic is implementable as written once its named M0 inputs land. Every AC maps to a module and a test; the data contracts match the real surfaces the design calls into (the LHC SDK at `packages/lhc`, the PI extension API at `@earendil-works/pi-coding-agent` v0.79.2, the completion API at `@earendil-works/pi-ai`). The tech-design questions are answered below, and the places where the design takes a position the epic left open are recorded as deviations with rationale.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:112:**Outgoing — inference, through PI:** the host-supplied `ModelCall` resolves `(provider, model)` via `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` and completes via `complete(model, context, options)` from `@earendil-works/pi-ai`, returning `Promise<AssistantMessage>`.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:141:All modules below nest within one of the three active surfaces. The package is a fresh scaffold (`packages/pi-lhc/` currently holds only `package.json`), so every module is NEW; the only EXISTS dependencies are the `lhc` workspace package and the PI/pi-ai packages.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:193:| `inference/model-call.ts` | NEW | Resolve (provider,model) via registry; complete; classify failures; multi-lane | PI modelRegistry, pi-ai | AC-4.1, AC-4.2, AC-4.3, AC-4.4 |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:359:LHC needs completions for its derivations and must get them through the user's existing PI auth, with no second login. The connector supplies one function at construction; LHC calls it with a `(provider, model)` pair and a single-turn message list and treats both strings as opaque routing keys. The function resolves the pair with `ctx.modelRegistry.find(provider, model)` and completes with pi-ai's `complete(model, context)`, returning the assistant text or a classified failure. Different derivation kinds can carry different pairs in the same session; the function routes each by its keys without interpreting them.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:370:  participant AI as pi-ai complete\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:374:    MC->>AI: complete(model, context)\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:543:| Adapter / Runtime Boundary | `inference/model-call.test.ts` | Each PI/pi-ai failure shape maps to the exact `ModelCallFailureKind` | TC may say \"error classified\"; the hazard is the precise runtime-error → code mapping |\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:599:**The critical mocking rule, applied:** mock at the external boundary, never at internal module boundaries. The external boundaries are the PI hook surface (fed by synthetic events and recorded corpora) and the `ModelCall`'s reach into PI's `modelRegistry` + pi-ai `complete` (supplied as a deterministic fake). Everything LHC runs real.\ndocs/specs/02-pi-lhc/01-connector-core/tech-design.md:604:| `modelRegistry` + pi-ai `complete` | Yes (the fake `ModelCall`) | External boundary — control completion text and failure shapes |\ndocs/specs/01-lhc-sdk/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/002-story-orchestrate-run.json:1:{\"command\":\"story-orchestrate run\",\"version\":1,\"status\":\"needs-user-decision\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"result\":{\"case\":\"completed\",\"outcome\":\"needs-ruling\",\"storyId\":\"05-message-edit-cascade\",\"storyRunId\":\"05-message-edit-cascade-story-run-001\",\"currentSnapshotPath\":\"/Users/leemoore/code/pi-long-horizon/liminal-context/packages/lhc/docs/02-specs/02-derivation-pipeline/artifacts/05-message-edit-cascade/story-lead/001-current.json\",\"eventHis